## Technologies

- **[FastAPI 0.109.0](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/)**: Modern, fast (high-performance) web framework for building APIs
- **[Uvicorn 0.27.0](https://www.uvicorn.org/)**: ASGI server for FastAPI
- **[Pydantic 2.5.3](https://docs.pydantic.dev/)**: Data validation and settings management
- **[SQLAlchemy 2.0.25](https://www.sqlalchemy.org/)**: ORM for database operations
- **[PostgreSQL](https://www.postgresql.org/)**: Open source relational database

## API Endpoints

The following endpoints are available:

### Root
- `GET /` - Application information
- `GET /health` - Health check

### API v1
- `GET /api/v1/health/` - Health check
- `GET /api/v1/health/detailed/` - Detailed health check
- `GET /api/v1/examples/` - List all examples
- `POST /api/v1/examples/` - Create a new example
- `GET /api/v1/examples/{id}` - Get a specific example
- `PUT /api/v1/examples/{id}` - Update an example
- `DELETE /api/v1/examples/{id}` - Delete an example
- `PATCH /api/v1/examples/{id}/toggle` - Toggle example active status

### API Documentation
- `GET /api/docs` - Interactive Swagger UI
- `GET /api/redoc` - Alternative ReDoc documentation
- `GET /api/openapi.json` - OpenAPI schema

## Adding Endpoints

1. Create a new endpoint file in `app/api/v1/endpoints/`
2. Add a router with the endpoint functions
3. Import and include the router in `app/routers/v1.py`

Example endpoint:

```python
from fastapi import APIRouter

router = APIRouter(prefix="/new-route", tags=["new-route"])

@router.get("/")
async def read_new_route():
    return {"message": "Hello from new route!"}
```

## Adding Models

1. Create a new model file in `app/models/`
2. Define your SQLAlchemy model

Example model:

```python
from sqlalchemy import Column, String, Integer
from .base import BaseModel

class NewModel(BaseModel):
    __tablename__ = "new_models"
    
    name = Column(String(255), nullable=False)
    value = Column(Integer, default=0)
```

## Database Configuration

### SQLite (Default)

No configuration needed. The database file will be created automatically at `sql_app.db`.

### PostgreSQL

Update `DATABASE_URL` in `.env`:

```
DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://user:password@localhost:5432/database
```

Install PostgreSQL adapter:

```bash
pip install asyncpg
```

### MySQL

Update `DATABASE_URL` in `.env`:

```
DATABASE_URL=mysql+aiomysql://user:password@localhost:3306/database
```

Install MySQL adapter:

```bash
pip install aiomysql
```

## Docker Deployment

### Build and Run with Docker Compose

```bash
# Build and start all services
docker-compose up -d --build

# View logs
docker-compose logs -f

# Stop all services
docker-compose down
```

### Using the Docker Image

```bash
# Build the Docker image
docker build -t fastapi-app .

# Run the container
docker run -p 8000:8000 \
  -e APP_NAME=MyApp \
  -e SECRET_KEY=your-secret-key \
  -e DATABASE_URL=your-database-url \
  fastapi-app
```

## Deployment Options

### Railway

```bash
# Install Railway CLI
npm install -g @railway/cli

# Deploy
railway init
railway add postgres
railway up
```

### Render

1. Create a new Web Service on Render
2. Connect your GitHub repository
3. Set the build command: `pip install -r requirements.txt`
4. Set the start command: `uvicorn main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port $PORT --workers 4`

### AWS Elastic Beanstalk

```bash
# Install EB CLI
pip install awsebcli

# Initialize EB
eb init -p python-3.11 fastapi-app --region us-west-2

# Create environment and deploy
eb create fastapi-env
```

### Google Cloud Run

```bash
# Build and push to Google Container Registry
gcloud builds submit --tag gcr.io/YOUR_PROJECT_ID/fastapi-app

# Deploy to Cloud Run
gcloud run deploy fastapi-app \
  --image gcr.io/YOUR_PROJECT_ID/fastapi-app \
  --platform managed \
  --region us-central1 \
  --allow-unauthenticated \
  --port 8000
```

## Authentication

The application includes JWT-based authentication utilities in `app/core/security.py`:

- `create_access_token()` - Create an access token
- `create_refresh_token()` - Create a refresh token
- `decode_token()` - Decode and verify a token
- `get_current_user()` - Dependency for getting the current user
- `get_optional_user()` - Dependency for optional authentication

Example usage:

```python
from fastapi import Depends, HTTPException, status
from app.core.security import get_current_user

@router.get("/users/me")
async def read_users_me(current_user: dict = Depends(get_current_user)):
    return current_user
```

